For the airline, a minute added to every turn takes delay off the rest of the aircraft's day only where a late inbound reaches into the turn, which was {{ v('ch8.binding_share') }} of turns in the reporting years. Counting the minute it saves on the next flight and the share that would have carried further down the day, a buffer minute saves {{ v('ch8.trade_overall') }} arrival minutes on average. {% if raw('ch8.trade_pays_airports') > 0 %}It pays for itself, saving more than the minute it costs, at {{ v('ch8.trade_pays_airports') }} of the busiest airports, led by {{ v('ch8.trade_best_airport') }} at {{ v('ch8.trade_best_saved') }} minutes per minute.{% else %}It does not pay for itself at any of the busiest airports on this count; the most it saves is {{ v('ch8.trade_best_saved') }} minutes per minute, at {{ v('ch8.trade_best_airport') }}, so a buffer is worth adding only where turns are reached far more often than average.{% endif %}

